n Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T10:40:40-07:00","id":1383793,"title":"","content":"I feel like vampires aught to have a psuedo-sexual attraction to tasty looking people <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've never felt that storytellers treat sex the way they do because they read it in the book. Either they think vampires have lots of fantastic sex because vampires are just damn sexy things, or they think vampires don't enjoy sex because they don't want to encourage the power-fantasy distractions of liberal minded horny players. The book carries no weight, it's all the storyteller's prerogative. I've played in games that might as well've been a pornographic adventure and games where the storyteller is barely comfortable with feeding.<br /> <br /> Personally I think vampires don't get that good feeling from the action, and instead draw pleasure from the power-fantasy/being adored/ the Imitation of life/ Sweaty people with fast heart rates taste better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-25-2020, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T10:56:20-07:00","id":1383798,"title":"","content":"I think it's largely up to storytellers.<br /> <br /> But yes, in my games, all vampires that can go through a phase of, &quot;Feeding on the yummy sexy people.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's part of growing up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T11:45:01-07:00","id":1383807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383761-v5-so-do-vampire-still-have-great-sex-or-no-sex?p=1383767#post1383767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the Giovanni. They're universally shit at vampire sex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey! Rude.<br /> <br /> But yes. The mechanics in the corebook say vampires can't have sex unless they're exceptionally humane, only fake it, and at a lower Humanity they can't even do that.<br /> <br /> \u2026and then the Cam book has a section narrated by Victoria Ash, describing what each Camarilla clan is like as a lover.<br /> <br /> \u2026and then Cults has an amusingly dark bit of fiction that involves two low-humanity necromancers (a Giovanni and a Pisanob) having sex the way mortals do and enjoying it.<br /> <br /> Personally, I just leave it up to the individual player and say some vampires like it, some don't. Sex is one of those things that seems like it doesn't really need hard mechanics attached; I'm more interested in what happens to the dynamics and relationships between the characters, than in how many successes you got on your &quot;fake orgasm&quot; roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T11:49:34-07:00","id":1383809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383761-v5-so-do-vampire-still-have-great-sex-or-no-sex?p=1383807#post1383807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey! Rude.<br /> <br /> But yes. The mechanics in the corebook say vampires can't have sex unless they're exceptionally humane, only fake it, and at a lower Humanity they can't even do that.<br /> <br /> \u2026and then the Cam book has a section narrated by Victoria Ash, describing what each Camarilla clan is like as a lover.<br /> <br /> \u2026and then Cults has an amusingly dark bit of fiction that involves two low-humanity necromancers (a Giovanni and a Pisanob) having sex the way mortals do and enjoying it.<br /> <br /> Personally, I just leave it up to the individual player and say some vampires like it, some don't. Sex is one of those things that seems like it doesn't really need hard mechanics attached; I'm more interested in what happens to the dynamics and relationships between the characters, than in how many successes you got on your &quot;fake orgasm&quot; roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think most of this is resolved by the Blush of Life being something that all vampires can do for just Rouse check roll, which DRAMATICALLY reduces the number of blood points you needed to spend to get everything going. Your heat beats, you can eat food, and you can also fuck in my opinion [I believe that is implied]. Any vampire can use the Blush of Life, regardless of humanity.<br /> <br /> I think the idea you have to high Humanity in order to have sex is also silly but that's what the rules say.<br /> <br /> The thing is, with the Pisanob, I also think that what qualifies as SEX is going to be up for debate. It's quite a large variety of activities and actions that go beyond penile penetrative sex.<br /> <br /> I mean, anyone with certain body parts and attributes should be able to have some form of it--whether they enjoy it or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T11:54:55-07:00","id":1383810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383761-v5-so-do-vampire-still-have-great-sex-or-no-sex?p=1383809#post1383809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, with the Pisanob, I also think that what qualifies as SEX is going to be up for debate. It's quite a large variety of activities and actions that go beyond penile penetrative sex.<br /> <br /> I mean, anyone with certain body parts and attributes should be able to have some form of it--whether they enjoy it or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but without going into too much explicit detail, the characters in Cults certainly do seem to enjoy it while also not being particularly humane. (It's not the main focus of the fiction piece, but it's still canon.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T12:15:00-07:00","id":1383815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383761-v5-so-do-vampire-still-have-great-sex-or-no-sex?p=1383769#post1383769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26067\" data-vbnamecard=\"26067\">Wingstorm</a><br /> <br /> Do you mind if I ask what page in DAV20 it talks about vampire sex? Thanks in advance to anyone who posts it as I'm too lazy to search for it. (hey at least I'm honest)</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the last paragraph of page 13 to the first paragraph of page 14 in V20DA.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T22:06:29-07:00","id":1384105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383761-v5-so-do-vampire-still-have-great-sex-or-no-sex?p=1383767#post1383767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the Giovanni. They're universally shit at vampire sex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but their partners either tell no tales or keep it in the family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T00:17:13-07:00","id":1384116,"title":"","content":"An angle I usually employ regarding vamps and sex is that Vampires don't embody the sin of lust, but of gluttony. Their inner beast wants to gorge and consume all they can get their hands on, be it blood or life or power.<br /> <br /> Taking this approach to sex, vampires aren't what I would describe as generous lovers. They want to consume everything their partner is and does. They don't sleep with people because they are horny, they sleep with them because they see the vibrant life in a person and want to partake in it in the most intense way they can think of. This is also why sex and torture are so closely related to the Toreador Antitribu <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So I would play sex not as a consequence of getting horny, but as a consequence of getting HUNGRY. Eat them, body and soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Furthermore, I believe Carthage should be destroyed.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23835-pang4","name":"pang4","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T02:22:05-07:00","id":1384132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383761-v5-so-do-vampire-still-have-great-sex-or-no-sex?p=1383767#post1383767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Sex is like pizza, even when it's not good, it's still kinda good.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>...let's just say I disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T05:48:46-07:00","id":1384173,"title":"","content":"The &quot;No sex please, we're vampires&quot; rule strikes me as making a nonsense of the Siren predator type. And &quot;You cannot have sex <i>per se</i>, but you can fake it with a roll&quot;, always reminds me of Frank Drebin in the Naked Gun saying, &quot;By the way, I faked my orgasms&quot;.<br /> <br /> I suspect that that rule will be pretty much universally ignored and junked in the next revision. Probably it was the writers going overboard with the whole, &quot;You are monstrous, you are inhuman, look at how cool my enormous angst is&quot; schtick. Personally, I'm sticking with the V20 and DA20 approach.<br /> <br /> My take: Kindred commonly perceive the urge to feed as sexual. The physical desire that they experience towards humans is hunger rather than lust, but they have no context for wanting to eat other humans, so they rationalize the feeding urge in sexual terms. Some may actually combine it with sex because of that association rather than out of inherent need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T06:26:27-07:00","id":1384176,"title":"","content":"I would say that vampires can still take an appreciation of other aspects of sex beyond the need to reproduce (which is clearly another drive for them). I think the ultimate sexual act for a vampire is their own \u2018embrace\u2019 but they probably still have enough sensitivity to respond to the other emotional, tactile and social aspects of what sex otherwise provides. A Toreador would probably consider the artistry involved, a Brujah would consider it a right, a Gangrel would recognize the animal passion, a Venture would enjoy the power, A Malkavian would laugh at the absurdity of it, and a Nosferatu would appreciate the attention. A Tremere might take notes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T09:33:36-07:00","id":1384203,"title":"","content":"Here's how I see it: in Anne Rice's novel, vampires were made sexless so many things could be explored utterly via metaphor. All the relationships in Interview are abusive in a way that making it about sexless vampires renders abstract and allows the audience to have a greater comfort level reading about. It's a lot like Star Trek in that way.<br /> <br /> Giving vampires the ability to have sex eliminates that abstraction. In novels, this is generally for one of two reasons. One is, as in the Necroscope books, the writer isn't interested in subtle metaphor, and wants to tell a story about monsters who are amplified conqueror aristocrats who rape and exploit and enslave and see ordinary people as nothing but resources to be used as food, clothing, furniture, fuel, soap, labor, and sex. It's less metaphor and more satire, parody, or caricature. Vampires as Orcs. Rather than metaphor, orc stories are about taking something that is subtle in real life and making a blatant, unsubtle caricature of it in fantasy form.<br /> <br /> The second reason some writers give vampires sex is they really just want to write an old fashion bodice-ripper about a sexy, powerful, brooding man that the audience-stand-in female is ravished by and who tames him, making him her devoted mate after she saves him from himself. Fifty Shades of Bloodsucker stuff.<br /> <br /> So the question is, do you want to deal with abusive things via subtle metaphor, satirize real life horrors via fantasy caricature, or play bodice: the rippering?<br /> <br /> If you want the first, then sexless vampires work best. You can explore extremely dark themes in a way that is no more uncomfortable than the four lights Star Trek episode.<br /> <br /> If you want to do satire, then vampires should not only be sexual, they should be superhumanly sexual, monstrous caricatures of every evil aristocrats and imperialists routinely committed, which includes a superhuman ability to commit rape.<br /> <br /> If you want to do a bodice-ripper, then they obviously need to be sexual, though not necessarily superhumanly so, just very high-end fantasy lover sexual. <br /> <br /> I think the White Wolf guys have always been more comfortable with the first. They want to deal with dark themes in a way that is, like the darker episodes of Star Trek, comfortable and safe because it is done using utterly abstract metaphors.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile you've got a lot of players who want to play Bodice: The Rippering or blatant satire games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T10:43:49-07:00","id":1384220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383761-v5-so-do-vampire-still-have-great-sex-or-no-sex?p=1384203#post1384203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the White Wolf guys have always been more comfortable with the first. They want to deal with dark themes in a way that is, like the darker episodes of Star Trek, comfortable and safe because it is done using utterly abstract metaphors.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile you've got a lot of players who want to play Bodice: The Rippering or blatant satire games.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue with this analysis is that a whole lot of White Wolf's published books say very clearly that vampires do have sex. Most infamously, there's <i>Eternal Hearts</i>, but more recently at least two of the published V5 books (Camarilla and Cults) mention it.<br /> <br /> And while modern White Wolf is doing better about this, I don't think &quot;dealing with dark themes in a way that is comfortable and safe&quot; is the best way to describe early-edition World of Darkness. Even just focusing on the sexual aspects, look at, say, the way Jan Pieterzoon used to get around his clan flaw. That's from canon material, not just &quot;players who want to play Bodice: The Rippering&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T11:20:38-07:00","id":1384227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383761-v5-so-do-vampire-still-have-great-sex-or-no-sex?p=1384203#post1384203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile you've got a lot of players who want to play Bodice: The Rippering or blatant satire games.</div> </div> </div> </div>By contrast, I think eliminating the need for sex to deal in metaphor is not necessary in an already R-rated game. Vampires have always been a metaphor to deal with sex, disease, rape, abusive relationships, and so on but there's no need to be PG-13 about the whole thing since Vampire: The Masquerade is a game for mature audiences to begin with. The metaphor can exist alongside the real thing.<br /> <br /> I mean, if I'm going to do a Black Dog-esque game about the player characters hunting down some human traffickers, I don't have to mince words.<br /> <br /> Obviously, YMMV at your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T06:29:48-07:00","id":1384400,"title":"","content":"Reading through everyone's thoughts on this matter, my take away is this. Vampires are like once mortals who pay a price/s for their immortality. The sun harm/kills them, they need blood, etc.<br /> One reminder of their lives as mortals is sex. <br /> <br /> By taking away sex, it kinda make them pointless as characters. You might as well just play really smart zombies that replace their hunger for Brains! With Blood!.<br /> Zombies, cos ultimately you are just playing an 1) undead with 2) a hunger issue, which 3)drives everything they do. <br /> <br /> So why bother with playing a vamp if there is no sex? Just be a really smart zombie. It's the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T16:34:12-07:00","id":1384529,"title":"","content":"It's worth defining &quot;great sex&quot; for this discussion.<br /> <br /> Vampires are predators, they use sexuality to exploit people, make victims think they (the vampires) are good in the sack with Presence and Dominate, and are incapable of orgasm on their own, except when they murder someone by draining them dry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T16:53:55-07:00","id":1384532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383761-v5-so-do-vampire-still-have-great-sex-or-no-sex?p=1384400#post1384400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading through everyone's thoughts on this matter, my take away is this. Vampires are like once mortals who pay a price/s for their immortality. The sun harm/kills them, they need blood, etc.<br /> One reminder of their lives as mortals is sex.<br /> <br /> By taking away sex, it kinda make them pointless as characters. You might as well just play really smart zombies that replace their hunger for Brains! With Blood!.<br /> Zombies, cos ultimately you are just playing an 1) undead with 2) a hunger issue, which 3)drives everything they do.<br /> <br /> So why bother with playing a vamp if there is no sex? Just be a really smart zombie. It's the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>On my end, I think it depends on how you view the Kiss. How pleasurable is the Kiss to both mortals and vampires. If you don't think of it as more pleasurable than heroin or sex but just think of it in terms of feeding then it's going to seem a lot more important to have sex as something that vampires have for the inherent power fantasy/mood. If the Kiss is every bit like sex to mortals, then does it really matter?<br /> <br /> There's also the issue of CAN vampires have sex versus do vampires ENJOY it? As well as the difference between pleasuring partners (w/ or without the Kiss).<br /> <br /> Honestly, I do think tying the ability to have sex to humanity is stupid as a mechanic. Sex is not really all that humane, just a thing mortals can do. It's like saying, &quot;Can vampires eat or shoot up?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383761-v5-so-do-vampire-still-have-great-sex-or-no-sex?p=1384529#post1384529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth defining &quot;great sex&quot; for this discussion.<br /> <br /> Vampires are predators, they use sexuality to exploit people, make victims think they (the vampires) are good in the sack with Presence and Dominate, and are incapable of orgasm on their own, except when they murder someone by draining them dry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, how is the Kiss?<br /> <br /> Does it feel like Great Steak or an orgasm?<br /> <br /> One of the reasons Herds are actually believable is because that mortals (at least in my games) are willing to bend over backwards to be food because it's so pleasurable. A vampire who has given up on almost all other elements of life will still probably get up in the morning because unless he's a Vegetarian, blood is enough to justify doing it.<br /> <br /> All vampires are addicts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T17:02:18-07:00","id":1384533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <di